{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0DSL", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-DM}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:610c023231b3dbe8fd7e415b0ff573aa63595764ac1b03415dce326fdff319af", "source_text": "The Deligne-Mumford locus", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6d8729371ce586171cb6c57c1ee2650677b00fe0ccfa25b2154fcdd3cd1e3aec", "unit_id": "tag:0DSL:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DSL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X = [\\Spec(\\mathbf{Z})/\\mathbf{G}_{m, \\mathbf{Z}}]$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cdc55ec22b9233702bd23ba29730a6208986727fde691c058422580408b3ace4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a5642479f381df0f976234bc4edd440f4495c90a450a3b63b0985a7b52d1f7b8", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nEvery algebraic stack has a largest open substack which is a\nDeligne-Mumford stack; this is more or less clear but we also\nwrite out the proof below. Of course this substack may be empty,\nfor example if <MATH_0001>.\nBelow we will characterize the points of the DM locus.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:06ad9fa93df5bad5396a218f394b37f0555b6bd577d0c681a09077b26c2dba6e", "unit_id": "tag:0DSL:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DSL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\mathcal{X}'' \\subset \\mathcal{X}' \\subset \\mathcal{X}\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X}''$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X}'$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-open-DM-locus}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d90789df61a6670a2bb1005a25c4838cc077909297d02032e72e391518f14838", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bcbffc7213cc2a2e9535b4482313c549138c4155002773359a1b257bd7d37256", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack. There exist open substacks\n<MATH_0002>\nsuch that <MATH_0003> is DM, <MATH_0004> is quasi-DM, and\nsuch that these are the largest open substacks with these properties.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:30222d5fdae8ad0db839bf49deeaf034b8663372d321c5aeede4f0f92aaf0fdb", "unit_id": "tag:0DSM:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DSL", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{U} \\subset \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{V} \\subset \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{W} \\subset \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$|\\mathcal{W}| = |\\mathcal{U}| \\cup |\\mathcal{V}|$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$V$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to \\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0008": "$V \\to \\mathcal{V}$", "MATH_0009": "$U \\amalg V \\to \\mathcal{W}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-DM}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{theorem-quasi-DM}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2879f1e7e6cc003ad7cf1a28cac3f7185f0830d4225c01d504b888ba0208c099", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:81b254a2d5765932121b4e4af61e6733f1fb30a29ac4ca9269fb9d52d33f2dc7", "source_text": "All we are really saying here is that if <MATH_0001>\nand <MATH_0002> are open substacks which are DM,\nthen the open substack <MATH_0003>\nwith <MATH_0004>\nis DM as well. (Similarly for quasi-DM.) Although this is a cheat, let\nus use Theorem <REF_0001> to prove this.\nBy that theorem we can choose\nschemes <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006> and surjective <ACCENT_0001>tale morphisms\n<MATH_0007> and <MATH_0008>.\nThen of course <MATH_0009> is surjective and <ACCENT_0002>tale.\nThe quasi-DM case is proven by exactly the same method using\nTheorem <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0f8c1ed83d256350bc8eea9f2957b8d6b62c5cabedd81c5af2ac8f91ad0cf3c9", "unit_id": "tag:0DSM:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DSL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\in |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0003": "$x : \\Spec(k) \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$G_x/k$", "MATH_0005": "$x$", "MATH_0006": "$x$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0008": "$G_x \\to \\Spec(k)$", "MATH_0009": "$x$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0011": "$G_x \\to \\Spec(k)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-points-DM-locus}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:202a71cdb886fb8e09bb62786d273feb8bdd6513cca57805d80e1ec70d64c1df", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:926e05ba5033908bc2efc2dab7a0ece06ab868835e8de8814f019a4bef38a2a6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack. Let <MATH_0002>\ncorrespond to <MATH_0003>. Let <MATH_0004>\nbe the automorphism group algebraic space of <MATH_0005>. Then\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002>  <MATH_0006> is in the DM locus of <MATH_0007>\nif and only if <MATH_0008> is unramified, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0009> is in the quasi-DM locus of <MATH_0010>\nif and only if <MATH_0011> is locally quasi-finite.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5686eaaf3100b6d6183c8523ae37176016d4699a6263f47ce605b5684044902b", "unit_id": "tag:0DSN:statement"}
